  "description": "Example of a SNOMED CT code system supplement used to share genus and species classifications for organisms. Each concept identifies the genus-level SNOMED CT concept the organism rolls up to and, where applicable, the species-level SNOMED CT concept. This example contains a small subset of the organism taxonomy used by the NHSN Hospital-Onset Bacteremia (HOB) measure, based on the [HOB organism taxonomy supplement](https://github.com/cqframework/dqm-content-cms-2026/blob/main/input/tests/HOBOrganismTaxonomySupplement/demo/CodeSystem-hob-organism-taxonomy.json).",
  "jurisdiction": [
    {
      "coding": [
        {
          "system": "http://unstats.un.org/unsd/methods/m49/m49.htm",
          "code": "840",
          "display": "United States of America (USA)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "purpose": "Illustrates sharing classification data (organism genus and species rollups) as properties defined in a code system supplement, so that logic can classify organisms consistently without embedding the classification in the logic itself.",
